72:/*
73: *  #250: data write-watchpoints. Break into the debugger when the guest
74: *  writes to a watched PHYSICAL address range (physical so a write via any
75: *  virtual alias �?" e.g. cached kseg0 vs uncached kseg1 on MIPS �?" is caught,
76: *  and 32-bit sign-extension of the vaddr is a non-issue). Opt-in; when
77: *  n == 0 the whole mechanism is a single compared-against-zero no-op on
