The watchpoints can see this physical write, but they are disabled during `step` and stop reporting once a debugger break is pending. The existing SGI probe uses `step`, so merely counting watchpoint messages there could falsely report zero. With an active observation window, the built-in watchpoint could answer “did any write attempt reach this range,” but it is not an exact call counter.
